# Performance benchmark: legacy PERI package (peri/pmb).
# Periodic 16^3 simple-cubic block (4096 nodes, horizon = 3 lattice spacings ->
# 122 bonds/node), run from the reference configuration so the per-step force
# cost is measured without dynamics/fracture.  Vary the model by editing the
# pair_style/pair_coeff lines (see README.md).

units           si
boundary        p p p
atom_style      peri
atom_modify     map array
neighbor        0.0005 bin
lattice         sc 0.0005
Lattice spacing in x,y,z = 0.0005 0.0005 0.0005
region          box block 0 16 0 16 0 16 units lattice
create_box      1 box
Created orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (0.008 0.008 0.008)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
create_atoms    1 box
Created 4096 atoms
  using lattice units in orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (0.008 0.008 0.008)
  create_atoms CPU = 0.001 seconds

pair_style      peri/pmb
pair_coeff      * * 1.6863e22 0.0015001 0.5 0.25
set             group all density 2200
Setting atom values ...
  4096 settings made for density
set             group all volume 1.25e-10
Setting atom values ...
  4096 settings made for volume

velocity        all set 0.0 0.0 0.0 units box
fix             1 all nve
timestep        1.0e-7
thermo          100
run             200

